From 2db8cd8e2dcc563640a5db9f2fd2ea081193fd85 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 26 Jun 2026 09:17:23 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 04198/11362] [outer-loop] S2-v2 + degenerate-pool detector,
 adversarially hardened (wf_3c4337f4)

Operator 'a+b': (a) pre-stage S2-v2 with diversity enforcement; (b) ship a degenerate-pool
detector. Adversarial verification (3 refuters, refuted_count=2) found the first cut was
GAMEABLE and the fixes are applied:

(b) adversarial_verify.check_engine_selection_candidate_diversity (DEGENERATE_CANDIDATE_POOL):
- INDEPENDENT FLOOR: required = max(5, ceil(0.6*total), declared) -- the agent's own
  min_heldout_games may only TIGHTEN, never lower it (closes the FN-3 self-declared-bar
  evasion: an artifact declaring min_heldout_games=1 no longer dodges; confirmed on exp4791).
- PASS not exempt (closes attack #3 PASS-bypass); negative-or-zero delta = no-value (FN-2);
  meaningful spread > 1e-3 not mere distinctness (FN-4 float-noise diversity); S2-scoped
  recognizer + any delta/margin key (FN-1 renamed-delta / FP-1 incidental-energy_delta);
  field-agnostic outcome metric (FP-2). 12 regression tests (incl. real exp4791 + every
  evasion). 71/71 guards green.

(a) S2-v2 .442 roadmap (exp4801-a1) hardening: independent-floor note, n_effective_games
  consistency, exact key (heldout_cell_recall), GENUINE-induction (no sabotage 0.0 engine),
  and BOUNDED-requires-positive-control (a documented headroom upper bound so BOUNDED means
  'energy could have won but didn't', not a degenerate non-test).

S2 recorded as INCONCLUSIVE (degenerate non-test), NOT bounded -- the energy direction is not
paused on it. Lints clean (exclusion-manifest, levelup); no /dev/mmcblk; space-substrate.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
